page(19,'Projected Financials','Extract from detailed P&L and CF statement from the Excel model. Base scenario; INR lakh; constant FY 2027–28 purchasing power. Annual amounts are rounded here; workbook calculations retain precision.',tables=[tab(['Fiscal year','Revenue','Pre-tax result','Operating CF','Cash before extra funding'],rows)],subsections=[sub('Scenario interpretation','Downside assumes zero device sales while showing the cost exposure of continued operation; it is not a recommendation to spend for ten years without buyers. Base annual sales rise arithmetically from 24 to 240. Upside rises from 60 to 600 with more assembly capacity, lower cost allowances and higher service attachment/renewal. These paths are illustrative and do not inherit any market-growth rate.','The base case requires approximately INR 19.76 lakh peak additional funding after the hypothetical pilot contribution; the upside still needs approximately INR 7.78 lakh at its peak. These figures are exposure calculations, not the proposed teacher ask. Income taxes, funding terms and full founder compensation remain outside the model’s stated scope.')])
page(20,'Projected Financials','Investment ask and funds deployment: proposed INR 44,470 pilot contribution, with no funds yet committed.',tables=[tab(['Use','INR','Release condition'],[['Setup and first two devices',16154,'First engineering stage'],['Next eight devices',24616,'Documented electrical/firmware/fit checks pass'],['Fulfillment allowance',1700,'Actual delivery need'],['Reserve held',2000,'Rework/warranty need, not automatic spending'],['Total funding envelope',44470,'Pilot only']])],subsections=[sub('Direct cash flow statement from the model','The direct cash method collects device receivables and service prepayments, then pays core purchases, fulfillment/reserves, service costs, operating labor, overhead and pilot expenses. The pilot reserve is held cash; commercial warranty allowance is conservatively expensed as a cash proxy.'),sub('First-year direct cash summary',tables=[tab(['Base FY 2027–28 flow','INR lakh'],[['Operating cash outflow, net',val(21,4)],['Hypothetical contribution financing',val(22,4)],['Closing cash before extra funding',val(23,4)],['Peak additional funding requirement',val(24,4)]])]),sub('Funding conditions and use of returns','No interest, equity percentage or repayment arrangement with the teacher is assumed. Confirm terms before funds are accepted. If commercialization later works, returns could come from distributable operating cash; acquisition is a possibility, not a promised exit. If evidence fails, stop new commitments and retain documented learning and reusable assets.')])
page(21,'Projected Financials','Graphs and charts: the following plots use the checked base scenario. They are expected outcomes under hypothetical inputs, not researched sales forecasts or actual results.')
page(22,'Thank you!','Cortex Sentinel requests support for a disciplined engineering pilot and an evidence-based commercial decision. The staged funding proposal limits exposure while the team checks reliability, customer usefulness and full delivery costs.','The decision sought is approval of the pilot purpose, funding conditions and stage-gate expectations. Successful demonstration alone will not establish customer demand or commercial viability.','Prepared by Kavyansh Kumar Baghel, Manas Sharma, King Kapoor, Nitin Kumar and Samarth Jain.')
checks=[['Problem','Sensitive-workstation access and environment-check workflow; Who We Are'],['How it is being addressed','Fingerprint, six checks, monitoring, TKC and planned recovery; Services/Processes'],['Competitors','Hello, Yubico, Defender and existing controls; Competitor Analysis'],['Un serviced Gaps','Three opportunity hypotheses and buyer complaints to test; Market Opportunities'],['USP','Intended integrated workflow; actual advantage remains unproven; Why US'],['Plan for 1 Yr','Two then eight engineering units, discovery and economic gates; Rollout plan'],['Plan for 3 Yrs','Conditional repeat delivery and wider India; no automatic expansion'],['Operations Plan','Build/test/install/recovery/support controls; Processes and Team Profile'],['Marketing Plan','Local discovery, demonstrations, website and CAC model; Marketing Strategy'],['Key Matrices','Break-even, capacity, contribution, CAC and retention sensitivities'],['Excel Sheet','Checked ten-year workbook; P&L, CF, balance drivers and charts reproduced above']]
page(23,'Final checklist','The original checklist labels are retained below. All items are addressed; completion of format does not turn classroom assumptions into observed evidence.',tables=[tab(['Template label','Where and how addressed'],checks)],subsections=[sub('Operations Plan','King verifies hardware and interfaces; Manas validates host/device state and recovery; Nitin maintains acceptance logs; Samarth records complete delivered costs; Kavyansh authorizes stage progression. If critical tests fail, pause the next eight units. No automatic Windows-lock guarantee is made when the host process is unavailable.'),sub('Risk and review discipline','Monthly review compares real cost, workload, buyer evidence and cash against assumptions. Trigger reassessment when contribution is nonpositive, cash cannot meet the next commitment, recovery permits unintended credential release, or customers cannot authorize installation. Update pricing, capacity, labor, inventory and funding together. Proposed mitigation reduces exposure but cannot eliminate technical, supplier or demand risk.')])
refs=['[1] Microsoft. Windows Hello for Business overview, updated 29 March 2026. https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/security/identity-protection/hello-for-business/','[2] Yubico. Security Key NFC product information. https://www.yubico.com/ch/product/security-key-series/security-key-nfc-by-yubico-black/ . Locale pricing is not Indian landed cost.','[3] Microsoft. Defender for Business India. https://www.microsoft.com/en-in/security/business/endpoint-security/microsoft-defender-business . Vendor listing inspected 14 November 2026: INR 250/user/month, annual billing, GST extra; different product scope.','[4] ICAI. September 2026 programme. https://www.icai.org/post/institute-program-sep2026 . Local institutional context only.','[5] RBI. UCB Cybersecurity, Technology: Risk, Resilience and Assurance Framework Directions 2026, 31 July 2026. https://www.rbi.org.in/Scripts/NotificationUser.aspx?Id=13616 . UCB-specific; not a universal SME requirement.','[6] Component listings inspected 14 November 2026: Probots ESP32 https://probots.co.in/esp32-30-pin-cp2102-development-board.html ; RoboPro R307 https://robopro.in/shop/r307-optical-fingerprint-sensor-module/ ; techiesms SH1106 https://techiesms.com/product/1-3-inch-oled-display-i2c-sh1106-white/ ; Probots PEM200 https://probots.co.in/surface-mount-plastic-enclosure-medium-pem200.html . Prices and compatibility require confirmation.','[7] Financial basis: Cortex Sentinel Financial Scenarios workbook, FY 2027–28 to FY 2036–37. Hypothetical scenarios; no observed sales or committed financing.','[8] Team and product scope: project-owner statements and accepted planning decisions recorded in November 2026. Product claims are user-reported unless explicitly labeled hypothetical. All synthetic market figures, ownership split, tagline, vision and planning schedules in this document are classroom assumptions.']
